{
  "id": "group-captivity",
  "title": "Group captivity",
  "summary": "Two batteries are each allowed both PV systems, and neither is individually stuck \u2014 but together they need every watt the two PV systems make. Deciding feasibility one sink at a time cannot see that; this is the case the max- flow solver exists for.",
  "shows": [
    "Feasibility is a property of groups of sinks, not of single sinks.",
    "A flexible sink must not take local power a tight group needs.",
    "When restrictions cannot all be honoured, the sink with the fewest permitted alternatives is served first and the deficit falls on the sinks that had somewhere else to go."
  ],
